---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import portrait from '../assets/photos/chifen-portrait.jpg';
import { site } from '../lib/site';

const journey = [
  {
    year: '2020',
    title: 'Founded Ayodah',
    body: 'Started a blood donor platform to close the gap between patients in urgent need and voluntary donors.',
  },
  {
    year: '2022',
    title: 'Won the Silicon Mountain Challenge',
    body: 'Ayodah took the prize, and kept growing to more than 400 registered donors and 310 donations across three partner hospitals.',
  },
  {
    year: '2022 to 2024',
    title: 'HND Nursing',
    body: 'Clinical training while running innovation and community projects on the side.',
  },
  {
    year: '2025',
    title: 'Moved deeper into digital health',
    body: 'Organised health innovation work and shifted from building around healthcare to building inside it.',
  },
  {
    year: '2026',
    title: 'BSc Nursing, and LifeDrop',
    body: 'Finished the AI clinical decision-making research at Buea Regional Hospital, launched LifeDrop, and placed third in the MTN YaMo Pitch Season 4.',
  },
  {
    year: 'Next',
    title: 'Master’s in health technology',
    body: 'Postgraduate study in health technology or digital health, peer-reviewed publication, and health-tech ventures that work across more of the continent.',
  },
];

const awards = [
  'Best Overall HND Student',
  'Best Nursing Student, HND',
  'Innovative Excellence Award',
  'Best Creative Thinker',
  'Proactive Student Award',
];

const skills = [
  {
    group: 'Healthcare',
    items: ['Clinical nursing', 'Emergency care', 'Health education', 'Clinical research'],
  },
  {
    group: 'Research and data',
    items: ['SPSS', 'KoboCollect', 'Excel', 'Data analysis', 'Scientific writing'],
  },
  {
    group: 'Technology',
    items: [
      'React Native',
      'Next.js',
      'Astro',
      'Tailwind',
      'n8n automation',
      'Prompt engineering',
      'AI workflow design',
      'Git and GitHub',
      'Figma',
    ],
  },
  {
    group: 'Communication',
    items: ['Content strategy', 'Brand development', 'Social media', 'SEO', 'Copywriting'],
  },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="Chifen Sama N. is a registered nurse and self-taught developer in Buea, Cameroon, building health technology for low-resource settings."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 pt-14 pb-16 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1.2fr_0.8fr] lg:gap-16">
      <div>
        <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-semibold sm:text-5xl">About</h1>

        <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate">
          <p>
            I am a registered nurse from the Cameroonian coast who taught himself to build
            software, and I have spent the last few years working at the seam between those two
            things.
          </p>
          <p>
            The seam is where most health technology fails here. Not because the ideas are bad,
            but because they are designed by people who have never watched a system break at two
            in the morning. I have. That is most of what I bring.
          </p>
          <p>
            The clearest version of this is blood. A family arrives, the ward has none, and the
            search falls on them: door to door, call by call, while the clock runs. The blood
            almost always exists somewhere in the same city. Nobody can find it in time. That is
            not scarcity, it is a coordination failure, and coordination is something you can
            build.
          </p>
          <p>
            So I built it, badly, and learned from that. Ayodah worked and still died at the
            install screen because I asked frightened people to go install an app. LifeDrop is the
            same network rebuilt where they already were, in WhatsApp. That correction is the
            single most useful thing I have learned about this work.
          </p>
          <p>
            My BSc research took the same instinct into AI. Everyone was debating whether
            Cameroonian health workers would accept AI in clinical decisions. I asked 387 of them.
            They are not resistant. They are under-trained and under-equipped, and they know it.
            The barrier they ranked highest was reliable electricity. Fear of losing their job
            ranked last of eighteen.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is the thread through all of it. Build for the ward that actually exists, on the
            power supply that actually exists, in the language people actually speak. Anything
            else is a demo.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="lg:pt-20">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl">
          <Image
            src={portrait}
            alt="Chifen Sama N."
            widths={[400, 640]}
            sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 80vw, 32vw"
            class="w-full object-cover"
          />
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-light">
          Chifen Sama N. Registered nurse, developer, based in {site.location}.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="border-y border-ink/10 bg-paper-dim/60">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl" data-reveal>The route here</h2>

      <ol class="mt-10 space-y-0">
        {
          journey.map((item, i) => (
            <li
              class="relative border-l border-ink/15 pb-9 pl-7 last:pb-0 sm:pl-9"
              data-reveal
              style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 60}ms`}
            >
              <span class="absolute top-1.5 -left-[5px] h-2.5 w-2.5 rounded-full bg-amber" />
              <p class="font-display text-sm font-semibold tracking-wider text-amber uppercase">
                {item.year}
              </p>
              <h3 class="mt-1.5 font-display text-xl font-semibold">{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-slate">{item.body}</p>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl" data-reveal>Awards</h2>
    <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        awards.map((award, i) => (
          <li
            class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded-xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/60 px-5 py-4"
            data-reveal
            style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 50}ms`}
          >
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-amber" />
            <span class="font-display font-medium">{award}</span>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-paper-dim/60">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl" data-reveal>What I work with</h2>
      <div class="mt-10 grid gap-9 sm:grid-cols-2">
        {
          skills.map((section, i) => (
            <div data-reveal style={`--reveal-delay:${i * 60}ms`}>
              <h3 class="font-display text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-amber uppercase">
                {section.group}
              </h3>
              <ul class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                {section.items.map((item) => (
                  <li class="rounded-full border border-ink/12 bg-white/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm text-slate">
                    {item}
                  </li>
                ))}
              </ul>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5 py-16 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold sm:text-4xl" data-reveal>Get in touch</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-lg text-slate" data-reveal>
      WhatsApp is fastest. Email works too, and I do read all of it.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2" data-reveal>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/60 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-amber uppercase">
          WhatsApp
        </h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
          {
            site.whatsapp.map((n) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={n.href}
                  class="font-display font-medium underline-offset-4 hover:text-amber hover:underline"
                >
                  {n.label}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink/10 bg-white/60 p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest text-amber uppercase">
          Email
        </h3>
        <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
          {
            site.emails.map((email) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`mailto:${email}`}
                  class="font-display font-medium break-all underline-offset-4 hover:text-amber hover:underline"
                >
                  {email}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
